Day 33: A Heart Set Free | Fifth Sunday of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“If the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed.”
Not someday.
Not eventually.
Now.

Welcome to Day 33 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into the deeply personal freedom Jesus offers — freedom from fear, from shame, from the quiet burdens you’ve learned to carry but were never meant to hold. Christ steps into the hidden places of your heart not to condemn, but to liberate.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that freedom is not the absence of struggle — it is the presence of Christ in the midst of it. He speaks truth where lies have taken root, love where shame has lingered too long, and freedom where you feel trapped.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why freedom in Christ is intimate, personal, and deeply healing

How Jesus meets you in the places you feel stuck or burdened

Why freedom is about releasing, not fixing yourself

A prayer to walk in Christ’s truth with confidence and joy

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, I release this to You.”

